+# Privacy and third-party review
+
+Review date: 2026-10-20. Scope: the source in this repository. This is an internal technical review, not an independent certification or legal assessment.
+
+## Data inventory and minimization
+
+This is a public static website. There are no implemented account, checkout, rewards, contact form, authentication, API, or database flows. Existing promotional links do not imply those services exist.
+
+- Incoming requests: the hosting infrastructure necessarily receives IP addresses, request paths, and browser headers. The Node application reads only method and URL for routing, does not log requests, and persists no visitor data. Query strings are ignored, never reflected, and never stored.
+- Browser: no client scripts, cookies, localStorage, sessionStorage, IndexedDB, service workers, identifiers, tracking pixels, or fingerprinting.
+- Application retention: zero persisted visitor records. Responses use no-store, including errors. This does not clear previously stored data or control infrastructure logs.
+- No data collection endpoints: only GET/HEAD are supported. No deletion/export endpoint is needed until there are actual visitor records.
+
+## Third-party inventory
+
+| Component | Before | Current treatment | Visitor disclosure |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Unsplash image | Browser request to images.unsplash.com disclosed IP, browser metadata and potentially referrer | Existing photo downloaded once into assets/coffee.jpg; served locally | No runtime provider request |
+| statikk / package registry | Unpinned pnpm dlx download on every start | Replaced by Node built-in HTTP server | No package download on start |
+| Fonts, analytics, ads, SDKs, embeds | None found | No runtime dependencies added; CSP rejects external resources | None from application code |
+| Hosting / TLS / CDN | Not configured in repository | Deployment operator must review | IP and connection metadata necessarily available |
+
+Image source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085 (Unsplash stock photo, retained from the original site).
+Asset is stored in the repository; no image API is used.
+
+Review this inventory before each integration change and at least quarterly. For every proposed vendor record its purpose, minimum fields, recipients/subprocessors, retention and deletion terms, security evidence, incident process, and applicable agreement. Prefer removing an integration or self-hosting static assets. Require explicit user action and clear disclosure before any optional embed or tracking loads. Do not claim a third party passed an independent audit without actual evidence.
+
+## Security controls
+
+- Exact route allowlist prevents publishing source files, dotfiles, dependencies, or traversing the filesystem.
+- All success/error responses carry CSP, no-referrer, disabled unused permissions, nosniff, frame protection, opener/resource isolation, and no-store.
+- CSP denies scripts, network connections, forms, plugins, frames, and all non-allowlisted resources. CSS is external to avoid unsafe-inline.
+- No cookie or auth scheme is invented for a static site. If sessions are introduced, use server-side authorization and __Host- cookies with Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/ and no Domain. Invalidate sessions on logout, provide data controls, and prohibit PII/tokens in browser storage or URLs.
+- Do not add raw request/error/violation logging. Reporting endpoints are intentionally absent: they would introduce collection of URLs and possible secrets. Any future telemetry needs redaction, a documented purpose, restricted access, and short retention.
+- Node must stay on a supported, security-patched release. No third-party application packages remain.
+
+## Deployment
+
+Run with Node 22+ using npm start (PORT defaults to 11222). The Node listener is HTTP; terminate TLS at a trusted reverse proxy, restrict direct public access to the origin, and enforce HTTP-to-HTTPS redirects at that edge.
+
+After confirming HTTPS is enforced, set HTTPS_ONLY=true. This enables upgrade-insecure-requests and a cautious HSTS max-age=300. Increase the HSTS duration after validating the domain; subdomain enforcement and preload require a separate domain-wide review. Do not trust arbitrary X-Forwarded-Proto values.
+
+Proxy/CDN responses, including redirects and errors generated upstream, must preserve equivalent security headers. Serving these files via another static host bypasses server.mjs and requires configuring the same headers there.
+
+Before production, the operator must identify the host and any subprocessors, disable unnecessary access logs, redact query strings/IPs where possible, define a necessary retention period and automated deletion, restrict log access, and publish a real operator privacy contact and host-specific retention details in privacy-policy.html. Those infrastructure settings and contact details are not available in this repository.
+
+## Repeatable verification
+
+Run npm test. Tests exercise real local HTTP responses, resource resolution, security headers on success and failure, unsafe method rejection, source/path isolation, HTTPS configuration, and the absence of third-party resource loading and browser persistence in the published source. No browser or external audit service is required. This source review does not verify a deployed proxy or third-party logging behavior.
+
+References: [MDN CSP](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP) and [OWASP Third Party JavaScript Management](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Third_Party_Javascript_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html).
